			"notes": "Many new animations!\n\nTouch'n Motion compatibility! (this was very difficult to achieve)\n\nADDED\n\n- Added Touch'n Motion compatibility.\n- Added rowing animations for boats and bamboo rafts.\n- Added swimming attack animations for punches, swords, axes, spears and items.\n- Added swimming poses for drawing a bow, loading a crossbow and aiming a loaded crossbow.\n- Added a new Axe attack type with its own attack combo.\n- Added a new Stab attack type. Items can use it through the item attack actions config.\n- Added Vanilla Backport spear compatibility. Spears use the Stab attack type.\n- Added Better Mob Combat compatibility.\n- Added a \"Better Mob Combat Animations\" setting to choose between Better Mob Combat's attacks and Mo'Bends' attack animations for mobs.\n- Added a \"Zombie Fist Attacks\" setting that lets zombies have punch animations.\n- Added Leaning Or Not compatibility.\n- Added Villager Recruits compatibility.\n- Added Valarian Conquest compatibility.\n- Added [ASW] Adaptive Skin Weathering compatibility.\n\nCHANGED\n\n- Revamped the config screen!\n- The spin attack is now off by default.\n- With Better Combat, Mo'Bends weapon animations now match the attack speed of the weapon.\n- With Better Combat, axes now use Mo'Bends' axe animations.\n- Zombie attacks now start from Mo'Bends' attack timer instead of the vanilla arm swing.\n- Armor now draws every part its model leaves visible.\n- Armor now uses each mob's own armor models instead of always using player-shaped ones.\n- Held items are now drawn through the same item renderer call as vanilla.\n\nFIXED\n\n- Fixed Better Combat attacks not playing for axes.\n- Fixed using a Riptide Trident underwater turning the player upside down.\n- Fixed the player floating above the water when sprint swimming.\n- Fixed the body jolting when going from swimming to a fighting stance.\n- Fixed helmets not covering the head of villager-type mobs.\n- Fixed GeckoLib armor not following Iron's Spells casting animations.\n- Fixed The Beyond's Ether Cloak shoulder pieces not rendering.\n- Fixed Immersive Blood Splatters blood flickering on Mo'Bends models.\n- Fixed Hackers 'n Slashers swords not hitting entities when using the Mo'Bends player model.\n- Fixed the player lying flat while flying during a Hackers 'n Slashers animation.\n- Fixed Mekanism Jetpack showing a missing texture on NeoForge.\n- Fixed RPG Series armor showing missing textures on NeoForge."
		},
